    {
      "id": "n1", "x": 30, "y": 500, "color": "blue",
      "anchorStates": [], "anchorTransitions": [],
      "text": "Adds a+b in place by transferring one unit at a time: decrement the right number, increment the left, repeat until the right number is all zeros — then erase it and the +. The sum materializes where a used to be."
    },
    {
      "id": "n2", "x": 880, "y": 150, "color": "green",
      "anchorStates": [], "anchorTransitions": [],
      "text": "Run 1011+11 and let it play: the highlight pulses around the ring once per transferred unit. A calculator built from a tape and eight states."
    },
    {
      "id": "n3", "x": 880, "y": 350, "color": "orange",
      "anchorStates": [], "anchorTransitions": [],
      "text": "The tape has no room left of cell 0, so give the left number a spare leading 0 if it might overflow: 0111+1, not 111+1."
    }
  ],
  "meta": {
    "title": "Binary addition a+b",
    "blurb": "Computes a+b on the tape by transferring one unit per lap: decrement b, increment a, repeat; when b hits zero it is erased and the sum sits where a was.",
